name prosocial-dialog-dialogues
# A JSON object on every line. The dataset card: `context` "the potentially unsafe utterance"; `safety_label` "the
# final verdict of the context according to `safety_annotations`"; `safety_annotations` "raw annotations from three
# workers". So an object is the thing its "context" names, and every other member is said of it.
# The card: `dialogue_id` "the dialogue index", `response_id` "the response index", `episode_done` "an indicator of
# whether it is the end of the dialogue". A line is one turn of a dialogue; until the engine reads a dialogue as the
# progression of its turns, the indexes are keys and episode_done is read by nothing.
match train.json test.json valid.json
format json
tier record by \n

thing record context
key record dialogue_id
key record response_id
content context response rots safety_label safety_annotations safety_annotation_reasons source etc
omit episode_done
# The card's "Data Fields":
#   `safety_label` {__casual__, __possibly_needs_caution__, __probably_needs_caution__, __needs_caution__,
#   __needs_intervention__}; `safety_annotations` "raw annotations from three workers: {casual, needs caution, needs
#   intervention}": labels, values of the set's own vocabulary.
value - safety_label safety_annotations
#   `response` "the guiding utterance grounded on rules-of-thumb (`rots`)"
relation "the guiding utterance grounded on rules-of-thumb" response
#   `rots` "the relevant rules-of-thumb for `text` *not* labeled as __casual__"
relation "the relevant rules-of-thumb" rots
#   `safety_annotation_reasons` "the reasons behind the safety annotations in free-form text from each worker"
relation "the reasons behind the safety annotations" safety_annotation_reasons
#   `source` "the source of the seed text that was used to craft the first utterance of the dialogue"
relation "the source of the seed text" source
#   `etc` "other information"
relation "other information" etc
attest record response rots safety_label safety_annotations safety_annotation_reasons source etc
